  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Additive inverses must differ only in sign. \\(0.5\\) and \\(-1/2\\) have the same absolute value and opposite signs. The pairs \\(2\\) and \\(1/2\\), and \\(-3\\) and \\(1/3\\), are reciprocals or are neither additive inverses nor reciprocals. Since \\(-(-4)=4\\), those two numbers are equal.",
